Z||000004||AusFiero||05-03-2001||08:25 PM||||Has anyone ever seen the see through 1968 Camaro that GM produced?<P>It did the show circut in the late 60's (before my time for shows). It eventually made it's way to Australia for our car shows then disappeared without a trace for 30 years.<P>In 1999 a member of the Camaro & Firebird Club of Australia found the car in Melbourne TAFE (technical and further education, learning institution). It had been given to them by GM as a learning aid because GM didn't want to pay to ship it home (unlike the Aztecs they bought over for The Survivor series). <P>Anyway the car was dissasembled and spread through many different departments until found by the above Camaro nut. He convinced the TAFE to help him locate most of the pieces and sell it to him.<P>The new owner will have the car ready for the show circuit in about 2002, but I have seen photos of it so I will try to aquire them. Try being the operative word as the guy is pretty guarded about his car.<P>GM USA have shown great interest in his project and are going to pay for it to be shipped to the US to do the car show circuit when he completes restoration of it. The see through body panels aren't the only feature, it just has so many.<P>Not a Fiero I know but while we was on see through cars I thought it might be interesting. Amazingly quite a lot of your rare autos and memorabillia make there ways to our shores and just never get taken home again.<p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||1
